# WebUI React + TypeScript

Stack: **Vite SPA** + React 18 + TypeScript. Do **not** apply Next.js / App Router / RSC / Server Actions patterns.

## TypeScript

- Prefer explicit props types (`type FooProps = { … }` or `interface`) above the component.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and narrow. Prefer types from `@/lib/types` for API payloads.
- Prefer named exports for components and helpers (page entrypoints may re-export from `index.ts`).

## React

- Functional components + hooks only (class components only for rare error boundaries).
- Derive values during render; do not use `useEffect` to sync derived state into `useState`.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default — only when profiling or an existing pattern requires it.
- Keep event handlers and effects focused; extract hooks (`useX`) when logic is reused or crowds the component.
- Lists: stable keys (ids), never array index for reorderable lists.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Next/RSC mindset or derived-state effect
export default async function Page() { /* server component */ }
useEffect(() => setFullName(`${first} ${last}`), [first, last]);

// ✅ GOOD — Vite SPA client component
export function ChannelRow({ channel }: ChannelRowProps) {
  const fullName = `${channel.botName} · ${channel.id}`;
  return <div>{fullName}</div>;
}
```
